# ============================================================================
# company.rule  —  year + special-char + leetspeak mutations for CTF cracking
# ============================================================================
# Usage:
#   hashcat -a 0 -m <mode> hashes.txt companies.txt -r company.rule
#   (companies.txt = the one-word-per-line file from the gum script)
#
# Each line below is ONE rule = ONE candidate per input word. Hashcat cannot
# loop, so the full form x year x special matrix is spelled out explicitly.
#
# HOW TO MAINTAIN -------------------------------------------------------------
#   Years      : 2000-2030. To add a year, copy any 4 "$d" group and edit the
#                digits, e.g. 2031 -> $2$0$3$1
#   Specials   : none ! @ # $ % * - &   (append a new "$X" column to add one)
#   Case forms : c = Capitalise (Acme) | u = UPPER (ACME)
#   Leet form  : substitutions only, ORIGINAL CASE PRESERVED (no case function).
#                Map:  a/A->4  e/E->3  i/I->1  o/O->0   (s and t unchanged)
#                eBay -> eB4y, Company -> C0mp4ny, SIEMENS -> S13M3NS
#                Edit the substitution string to change the map.
#
# Columns per line:  [leet]  [year digits]  [special]
# ============================================================================

